<!-- CORE FEATURES -->
<section class="vexes-section" id="features">
  <div class="vexes-container-wide">
    <p class="section-label reveal">Core features</p>
    <div class="vexes-features-grid reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.05s;">
      <div class="vexes-feature-card">
        <h3>Pre-Install Guard</h3>
        <p>Intercepts <code>npm install</code> and analyzes new packages before they execute. Diffs lockfiles, blocks threats, then runs the real install.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vexes-feature-card">
        <h3>Verified Fix Recommendations</h3>
        <p>Every suggested upgrade is cross-checked against OSV to ensure the fix version isn't itself vulnerable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vexes-feature-card">
        <h3>CI/CD Integration</h3>
        <p>GitHub Actions annotations, SARIF output for Advanced Security, and watch mode for continuous monitoring.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vexes-feature-card">
        <h3>Fail Loud, Not Clean</h3>
        <p>If queries fail, vexes exits with code 2 and prints SCAN INCOMPLETE. Never silently reports clean on failure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vexes-feature-card">
        <h3>Zero Dependencies</h3>
        <p>The dependency chain is the attack surface. vexes has none. Acorn is vendored. SQLite is Node.js built-in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vexes-feature-card">
        <h3>Undisableable Signals</h3>
        <p>Critical signals like KNOWN_COMPROMISED and PHANTOM_DEPENDENCY cannot be turned off via config. They detect active attacks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

